{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"77600c9c-4d20-49f0-a68f-18d3ed3cae23","agentId":"abab904b048cba0e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: 1 search per fact, 5 checks, one 400px screenshot, report under 100 words. Do not edit cuore/app.py (report include lines), shop_* files (another agent), or mes-log-mcp/mes files other than NEW mes/tools_kb.py and mes/tool_usage.py (+ server.py tool registrations). Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; cuore FastAPI + Jinja (classes at the end of cuore/web/static/cuore.css, 44px targets); tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR. Related: mes/jobs.py (jobs with actions), mes/maintenance_specs.py and service_specs.py (jobs and torque keys), mes/drivetrain_specs.py, mes/parts.py, mes/experience.py (how-to links), cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/web/jobs_routes.py + templates/job.html.\n\nGoal: CUORE recommends the tools for each job and step, the mechanic records what he actually used at release, his preference and why, and whether to buy a different tool next time; the next identical job on a Stelvio shows that learning first. House rule: never invent sizes or specialist tool numbers: UNKNOWN with \"confirm on the car / service manual (TechAuthority)\"; cite sources (owner's manual, TSBs in mes/knowledge.py, forum/YouTube entries in mes/experience.py).\n\nBuild:\n1. mes/tools_kb.py: TOOLS (keyed) {name, kind: hand|torque|special|diagnostic|lift|consumable, spec (size/range if sourced), why, source, confidence} and JOB_TOOLS keyed by job/step (oil_change, spark_plugs, engine_air_filter, cabin_air_filter, brake_fluid incl. EPB service mode via MES/wiTECH, brakes_front/rear, transfer_case, drive_belt, battery_12v, evap: smoke test, ESIM test A (hand vacuum pump), purge valve actuation, quick-connect release, electrical inspection (DVOM, back-probe, wiggle), network: voltage-drop test, turbo_replacement incl. oil feed/return and coolant lines (flare-nut/crowfoot wrenches, line-fitting tools: sizes UNKNOWN unless sourced; note the risk of the wrong tool adding hours), zf8hp_fluid (fill adapter, temp read via MES/cuore), wheel/tyre (torque wrench 121 Nm), diagnostics (ELM327/STN on COM3, MES, wiTECH)): [{tool key, required: bool, alternatives: [keys], note}]. recommend(job_or_step) -> list.\n2. mes/tool_usage.py: JSONL <state>/tool_usage.jsonl rows {id, vin, job_id, step, at, by, tools_used: [{tool key or free text name, was_right: yes|no|unsure, note}], missing_tools: [text], would_buy: [{name, why}], time_min}; add/load(vin=None, step=None)/learn(step) -> aggregated: top tools used, flagged as wrong, buy suggestions with counts. MCP tools: tool_recommend(step), tool_usage_add(...), tool_learn(step).\n3. cuore/services/tools_kb_bridge.py + cuore/api/tools_kb.py (GET /tools-kb/recommend/{step}, GET/POST /vehicles/{vin}/tool-usage, GET /tools-kb/learn/{step}); report include line.\n4. UI (edit cuore/web/jobs_routes.py and templates/job.html, plus a NEW cuore/web/templates/_tools_panel.html): on the Job page step 3 (Tests & inspections) and step 5 (Repair actions) show \"Tools for this step\": recommended list with required/alternative chips, sourced notes, the learned \"what mechanics used last time / flagged wrong / suggested buys\"; at step 7 (Outcome & handover, before close) a mandatory \"Tools used\" review form: tick recommended tools used, add others, mark right/wrong/unsure with a reason, missing tools, would-buy with why, minutes spent; stored via tool_usage; the job cannot close until the review is saved (or explicitly skipped with a reason). Also show the panel on maintenance.html per item (recommend(job key)), compact.\n5. Tests (5): recommend(\"oil_change\") includes a torque wrench with the 20 Nm drain-plug key; turbo lines entry has UNKNOWN sizes with the TechAuthority note; usage add -> learn aggregates was_right=no and would_buy; job close blocked without the review, allowed after; job page shows the tools panel. Run + cuore/tests/check_jobs_page.py and check_api.py."},"uuid":"990403c7-82f1-4bc2-93ac-6cd2254ea5d0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T09:31:46.321Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
