{"parentUuid":"f5405c81-6f0e-4091-a400-423d6091bc46","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abab904b048cba0e3","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpYFxU2ediupEaA5YAWx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WS2J7VyGsgbLfrgW6k7b1u","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,40p' cuore/web/parts_routes.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2218,"cache_read_input_tokens":118333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WS2J7VyGsgbLfrgW6k7b1u":{"command":"cd /c/Users/User/mcp-servers && sed -n '1,40p' cuore/web/parts_routes.py"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01WS2J7VyGsgbLfrgW6k7b1u":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1d9771a8-00b1-454f-a274-a0a26b4fac81","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfpYFxDu8SL7pdUoGHLXZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f82fd4a4-79a4-4b57-b8a6-8c2323ec79fc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T09:34:04.529Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"f82fd4a4-79a4-4b57-b8a6-8c2323ec79fc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8f581852-d8cf-4378-ac54-0005e1b4e468","agentId":"abab904b048cba0e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WS2J7VyGsgbLfrgW6k7b1u","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"``GET /v/{vin}/parts``: the parts catalog page -- search box, grouped by\njob, each part rendered through ``_part_card.html``.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore.web.dashboard_routes``/``service_routes``/\n``timeline_routes`` (all built the same way, concurrently with other\nagents): reuses ``_dossier``/``_page``/``_set_active_vehicle``/\n``_vehicle_bar`` from :mod:`cuore.web.routes` by import rather than\nduplicating that plumbing.\n\nRegisters a ``parts_for`` Jinja global the same way\n:mod:`cuore.web.timeline_routes` registers ``code_feel`` -- except on *both*\n``Jinja2Templates`` instances this feature's pages use: ``cuore.web.routes``'s\n(for ``code.html``) and ``cuore.web.service_routes``'s, a separate instance\n(for ``maintenance.html``/``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html``) -- the\nsame two-environments wrinkle :mod:`cuore.web.experience_globals` already\ndocuments and works around for ``experience_links``. So\n``{% if parts_for is defined %}`` resolves true on every page that wants it,\nwhichever of those two environments rendered it.\n\nThe data contract lives in :mod:`cuore.services.parts_bridge` (``part(key)``,\n``parts_for_code(code)``, ``parts_for_job(job)``, ``all_parts()``,\n``search_parts(q)``), built in parallel with ``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` --\nsee that bridge's docstring for the fixture it falls back to until that\nmodule lands.\n\nNot registered on the app here -- ``app.py`` is owned by another agent\nwhile this was built. The two lines needed there (next to the other ``web``\nrouter imports/includes):\n\n    ``from .web import parts_routes``\n    ``app.include_router(parts_routes.router)``\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"54005fad-5e97-450f-8e60-82f7bc1a96db","timestamp":"2026-10-08T09:34:05.155Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\"\"\"``GET /v/{vin}/parts``: the parts catalog page -- search box, grouped by\njob, each part rendered through ``_part_card.html``.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore.web.dashboard_routes``/``service_routes``/\n``timeline_routes`` (all built the same way, concurrently with other\nagents): reuses ``_dossier``/``_page``/``_set_active_vehicle``/\n``_vehicle_bar`` from :mod:`cuore.web.routes` by import rather than\nduplicating that plumbing.\n\nRegisters a ``parts_for`` Jinja global the same way\n:mod:`cuore.web.timeline_routes` registers ``code_feel`` -- except on *both*\n``Jinja2Templates`` instances this feature's pages use: ``cuore.web.routes``'s\n(for ``code.html``) and ``cuore.web.service_routes``'s, a separate instance\n(for ``maintenance.html``/``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html``) -- the\nsame two-environments wrinkle :mod:`cuore.web.experience_globals` already\ndocuments and works around for ``experience_links``. So\n``{% if parts_for is defined %}`` resolves true on every page that wants it,\nwhichever of those two environments rendered it.\n\nThe data contract lives in :mod:`cuore.services.parts_bridge` (``part(key)``,\n``parts_for_code(code)``, ``parts_for_job(job)``, ``all_parts()``,\n``search_parts(q)``), built in parallel with ``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` --\nsee that bridge's docstring for the fixture it falls back to until that\nmodule lands.\n\nNot registered on the app here -- ``app.py`` is owned by another agent\nwhile this was built. The two lines needed there (next to the other ``web``\nrouter imports/includes):\n\n    ``from .web import parts_routes``\n    ``app.include_router(parts_routes.router)``\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom