{"parentUuid":"cdba90c1-a87a-4e3f-8d86-4f7ac47de61b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abab904b048cba0e3","attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"Orchestrator, add to your scope (same 5-check budget, +2 checks max): (1) Garage tool INVENTORY in mes/tool_usage.py (or a small mes/tool_inventory.py): JSONL <state>/tool_inventory.jsonl rows {tool key or name, status: owned|borrowed|rental|not_owned|on_order, model, bought_on, cost, note}; set/list; MCP tool_inventory_set/list; a form on the tools panel (\"I have this / I don't\"). (2) recommend(step) results carry `have: owned|borrowed|not_owned|unknown` from the inventory, and when a REQUIRED tool is not owned the panel shows a DECISION card: when in the diagnosis this tool is used (for EVAP smoke test: after the recirculation quick-connect check S2125000002 and purge/vent KOEO actuation, before condemning canister/ESIM; cite mes/knowledge.py and docs/research/EVAP_SMOKE_TEST.md), alternatives (borrow, rental, dealer, or a different test), how often it will be needed (EVAP codes are common on Giorgio: cite forum/YouTube entries in mes/experience.py if they exist, else say unknown), and sourced cost options: e.g. smoke machine low-cost (~$80-150 class) vs professional (~$700-1,200 class, with built-in pressure gauge/flow meter, UV dye) with one source URL each and the practical difference for small leaks (0.020 in, P0456) if sourced; the mechanic records his decision (buy|borrow|rent|skip + why) in tool_usage.would_buy. Never invent prices: give a sourced range or UNKNOWN. (3) The worked example must appear on the Stelvio's EVAP steps (smoke test and ESIM Test A: hand vacuum pump).","source_uuid":"df6a7ef8-00da-4b6f-ae4d-9d89f9062f4e","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"isMeta":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6891a8b6-74c1-4006-835d-4ba38f1df919","timestamp":"2026-10-08T09:45:45.609Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe coordinator sent a message while you were working:\nOrchestrator, add to your scope (same 5-check budget, +2 checks max): (1) Garage tool INVENTORY in mes/tool_usage.py (or a small mes/tool_inventory.py): JSONL <state>/tool_inventory.jsonl rows {tool key or name, status: owned|borrowed|rental|not_owned|on_order, model, bought_on, cost, note}; set/list; MCP tool_inventory_set/list; a form on the tools panel (\"I have this / I don't\"). (2) recommend(step) results carry `have: owned|borrowed|not_owned|unknown` from the inventory, and when a REQUIRED tool is not owned the panel shows a DECISION card: when in the diagnosis this tool is used (for EVAP smoke test: after the recirculation quick-connect check S2125000002 and purge/vent KOEO actuation, before condemning canister/ESIM; cite mes/knowledge.py and docs/research/EVAP_SMOKE_TEST.md), alternatives (borrow, rental, dealer, or a different test), how often it will be needed (EVAP codes are common on Giorgio: cite forum/YouTube entries in mes/experience.py if they exist, else say unknown), and sourced cost options: e.g. smoke machine low-cost (~$80-150 class) vs professional (~$700-1,200 class, with built-in pressure gauge/flow meter, UV dye) with one source URL each and the practical difference for small leaks (0.020 in, P0456) if sourced; the mechanic records his decision (buy|borrow|rent|skip + why) in tool_usage.would_buy. Never invent prices: give a sourced range or UNKNOWN. (3) The worked example must appear on the Stelvio's EVAP steps (smoke test and ESIM Test A: hand vacuum pump).\n\nAddress this before completing your current task.\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
